Allan asks: 
> Why doesn't Nethack give directions for when you are blind or are faced
>by an invisible opponent. Surely your character can tell which way the
>blows are coming from. Also why don't some monsters show up when I put on
>a blindfold even though I have eaten a floating eye & gained telekenesis.

Probably not spoilers, but who really knows?
 

Maybe you can tell where the blows are coming from, maybe not.  A bash
over the top of the head would be tough to place with precision.  If
blind you should head for a corridor and thus curtail the number of
directions from which you can be attacked.  Or just run in a straight
line for a while, then back the other way, as your pursuer always
seems to lock on right behind you. 

You mean telepathy; telekinesis is the ability to move objects around
without touching them.  When you have telepathy you're detecting other
creatures' minds.  Some monsters are pretty mindless and thus invisible
to ESP.  These include zombies and molds and a few others that I don't
feel like looking up right now; you get the idea.

